.TH CTHRPOOL_FUTURE_CREATE_DETACHED 3 "2026-09-21" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cthrpool_future_create_detached \- create a standalone future with no pool or queued task
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

cthrpool_future *cthrpool_future_create_detached(char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a future that no cthread_pool task queue is behind. A
producer outside the pool, such as an event-driven engine that is not
itself a cthrpool worker, must call cthrpool_future_fulfill exactly once
to deliver the result.

On success the future has a reference count of 2, the same convention
as with cthrpool_submit_future: the caller holds one reference, which
cthrpool_future_free releases, and the producer holds the other one,
which cthrpool_future_fulfill releases. Each cthrpool_future_get call that
runs on the future adds one more for its duration.

The struct is freed once every reference is gone, in whatever order
they go. cthrpool_future_free can come before cthrpool_future_fulfill, and
either call can come while other threads still wait in
cthrpool_future_get, exactly as with a future that a pool is behind.

The function always uses the standard malloc and free and never a
custom allocator, the same as the futures of cthrpool_submit_future.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
err_str   Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
          (pass NULL to ignore)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a new cthrpool_future handle (not yet done) on success.
Returns NULL on allocation failure.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cthrpool_future_fulfill (3),
.BR cthrpool_future_get (3),
.BR cthrpool_future_done (3),
.BR cthrpool_future_free (3)
